      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Referred shoulder pain is an important yet potentially distracting sign of serious intra-abdominal illness. A case is presented wherein shoulder pain preceded by several hours the onset of abdominal pain in a teenage girl with gastric perforation. The range of causes of gastric perforation and the pathophysiology of referred shoulder pain are discussed."},
